# Canonical production-identity environment variables — ONE definition.
#
# These name a running production (or any specific) gateway instance: its ERTS
# paths, its release identity, and its instance selectors. They must never be
# INHERITED by a spawned session (R3), never be a DB env overlay (R9), and never
# leak into a source `mix test` run (verify_mix.sh). This file is the single
# source of truth so the three consumers cannot drift.
#
# Consumers:
#   - lib/tightbeam/production_identity_env.ex  (parsed at compile time; R3 + R9)
#   - scripts/verify_mix.sh                     (parsed at run time; source-test scrub)
#
# Format: one entry per line. `prefix <STR>` matches any var name starting with
# STR; `exact <NAME>` matches that var name exactly. Blank lines and lines
# beginning with `#` are ignored.
#
# NOTE the SESSION identity vars TIGHTBEAM_HOME / TIGHTBEAM_MACHINE /
# TIGHTBEAM_LINEAGE / TIGHTBEAM_URL are deliberately NOT here: they are
# per-session and are re-provided to spawned children, never a production leak.
prefix RELEASE_
exact ROOTDIR
exact BINDIR
exact TIGHTBEAM_BASE_DIR
exact TIGHTBEAM_PORT
exact TIGHTBEAM_NODE
